Description: CloudDeploy NVIDIA private HDR/PQ baseline for KWin 6.4.x
 Adds a runtime opt-in (KWIN_CLOUDDEPLOY_NVIDIA_PRIVATE_HDR=1) that, when the
 GPU is NVIDIA, skips the standard connector HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA and
 Colorspace=BT2020_RGB writes (NVIDIA's atomic check rejects them on the
 forced/headless DRM virtual output) and instead drives NVIDIA private
 properties:
   CRTC NV_CRTC_REGAMMA_TF        = PQ
   primary plane NV_INPUT_COLORSPACE = BT.2100 PQ
   primary plane NV_PLANE_DEGAMMA_TF = PQ
   primary plane NV_HDR_STATIC_METADATA = blob 0
 Empirically this is the configuration that produced KScreen reporting
 "HDR: enabled" + "Wide Color Gamut: enabled" on the live Ubuntu 25.10 /
 Plasma 6 / NVIDIA 580 VM. NV_HDR_STATIC_METADATA stays blob 0 by default
 because every variant that set it tripped nvKms->applyModeSetConfig.
Author: CloudDeploy
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-05-14

